Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:43:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 19/25] fix(geometry): keep the glass bar inside the app's own
 window

On the fold's inner display (portrait) and in Meituan's parallel window the
content view is narrower than displayMetrics, yet the floating-bar width
took the larger of the two. The bar was therefore laid out at display
width (1712 px over a 1179 px window), overflowing one side and dragging
its icons out of the window.

The bar now uses the intersection of the content width and the display
width, and the bottom gap uses the same rule for height. A bounded
[BarGeometry] report prints content/display/slots whenever a live width
change lands, so a future overwidth can be read from logcat.
